20,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It seems joint ventures here struggle with ownership and rotas. Also, home visits have a high failure rate due to access issues.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Interestingly, a previous call-back trial significantly reduced readmissions for the elderly, but the booking system fails to record any work without a fixed slot.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We have a serious nursing shortage and high agency costs, but the midwifery rota actually has some unusual slack.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The budget is tighter than we thought, and we only earn regional funds for on-site sessions. Off-site work is essentially unfunded.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Our parking and rooms are already at capacity by mid-morning, and external data agreements take over a year to finalize.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, if off-site work isn't funded, that makes home-based programs very risky.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Misaki, the midwifery slack is a rare opportunity. Does that make a perinatal service viable?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"It might. Compared to the ward vacancies, it's the only area where we aren't already drowning.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, if the rooms are full, any program requiring new on-site space will fail or cost us more from the reduced budget.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Shizue,,Exactly. We cannot afford to add more pressure to the parking or the booking system.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, you mentioned the call-back trial worked. Could we adapt that without needing new rooms?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"Perhaps, but if it's not a fixed appointment, it disappears from the records, making it hard to justify.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Misaki,,A perinatal service could potentially use existing spaces if the midwifery team is underutilized.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Shion,,We need something that generates revenue or uses existing slack. A home-visit team sounds like a financial black hole.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Shizue,,And the data agreements make coordinating with outside surgeries a nightmare.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Midori,,I'm leaning away from anything that relies on outside partners or home visits.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. The evidence for elderly readmission is strong, but the logistics are a mess.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Misaki,,The midwifery slack is the most stable resource we have right now.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Logically, the perinatal service is the only one that fits the staffing and budget constraints.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It seems the most absorbable option for our current infrastructure.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
